# Graphify — Query Before You Read

This project has a [Graphify](https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify) knowledge graph at `graphify-out/graph.json`.

**MANDATORY: Before using Read, Grep, Glob, or Bash to explore the codebase, run Graphify first:**

```bash
graphify query "<question>"   # scoped subgraph for architecture/behavior questions
graphify path "<A>" "<B>"     # dependency path between two symbols
graphify explain "<concept>"  # all nodes related to a concept
```

Or use project scripts:

```bash
pnpm graphify:update          # refresh graph after code changes (AST-only, no API cost)
pnpm graphify:build           # full rebuild if graph.json is missing
```

This applies to **you and every subagent** you spawn. Include this rule explicitly in subagent prompts that involve code exploration. Do not skip Graphify because files are "already known" — the graph surfaces cross-file dependencies and INFERRED edges that grep and Read cannot find.

## When to use Read/Grep/Glob directly

1. Graphify already oriented you and you need exact lines to edit or debug
2. `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist — run `pnpm bootstrap` or `pnpm graphify:build` first
3. You are editing a file you already have open with full context

## After code changes

- After modifying source: `pnpm graphify:update`
- After `git pull` or merge: graph refreshes automatically via `.husky/post-merge` (or run `pnpm graphify:update` manually)
- Graph outputs are gitignored — each developer regenerates locally via bootstrap and post-merge

## Reference files

| File | Use |
|------|-----|
| `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` | Broad architecture review only when query/path/explain are insufficient |
| `graphify-out/graph.html` | Interactive visualization (when generated via `pnpm graphify:viz`) |
| `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` | Agent-crawlable wiki (when `--wiki` was used) |

Prefer `graphify query` over reading raw files or the full report.

## Project hotspots (Better Auth boilerplate)

- **Auth**: `graphify explain "auth.ts"`, `graphify query "Better Auth sign in flow"`
- **Database**: `graphify explain "db.ts"`, `graphify path "User" "Session"`
- **Route protection**: `graphify explain "middleware.ts"`, `graphify explain "auth-guard.ts"`
- **API routes**: `graphify query "auth API route handler"`

## Subagent template

When launching explore/review subagents:

> Run `graphify query "<task-specific question>"` before reading source files. Run `pnpm graphify:update` if the graph may be stale.
